.TH HOMED 8 "October 2026" "homed 0.2.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
homed \- NSS-backed org.freedesktop.home1 D-Bus compatibility service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homed
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homed
provides a limited, non-systemd implementation of the
.BR org.freedesktop.home1
D-Bus API for accounts visible through the system's Name Service Switch (NSS).
It owns the system-bus name
.BR org.freedesktop.home1
and exports the manager object at
.BR /org/freedesktop/home1 .
The daemon is intended as a compatibility layer for systems such as Slackware
that do not use systemd.
.PP
This release is not a full replacement for systemd-homed. It reads account
information from NSS/passwd and does not create or manage home storage, perform
encryption, or activate login sessions. The daemon currently requires root.
.SH MANAGER METHODS
The manager object currently implements these methods:
.TP
.B GetHomeByName(user_name)
Looks up an NSS account by name and returns its UID, state, GID, real name,
home directory, shell, and per-home object path.
.TP
.B GetHomeByUID(uid)
Looks up an NSS account by numeric UID and returns its name, state, GID, real
name, home directory, shell, and per-home object path.
.TP
.B ListHomes()
Returns the NSS-visible accounts and their basic account information. These
entries represent NSS accounts, not necessarily managed home areas.
.TP
.B GetUserRecordByName(user_name)
Returns a user-record dictionary derived from NSS fields.
.TP
.B GetUserRecordByUID(uid)
Returns a user-record dictionary for the specified UID.
.TP
.B GetUserRecordByPID(pid)
Reads the real UID from the process status file under
.I /proc
and returns the corresponding NSS user record.
.PP
The user-record dictionary currently includes
.BR userName ,
.BR uid ,
.BR gid ,
.BR realName ,
.BR homeDirectory ,
.BR shell ,
.BR service ,
and
.BR disposition .
The service is reported as
.BR nss
and the disposition as
.BR regular .
These records return
.B true
for the
.I incomplete
output because NSS does not provide the managed-home metadata, secrets,
bindings, or signatures required for a complete systemd-homed user record.
.TP
.B AutoLogin
The manager exposes this read-only property as an empty array.
.SH PER-HOME OBJECTS
Each NSS account discovered by the daemon is represented at
.BR /org/freedesktop/home1/home/_UID ,
where
.I UID
is the account's numeric UID.
The
.B org.freedesktop.home1.Home
interface exposes the read-only properties
.BR UserName ,
.BR UID ,
.BR GID ,
.BR RealName ,
.BR HomeDirectory ,
.BR Shell ,
.BR State ,
and
.BR Service .
The current state is reported as
.B inactive
and the service as
.BR nss .
.PP
The interface declares
.BR Activate ,
.BR Deactivate ,
.BR Lock ,
.BR Unlock ,
and
.BR Resize
methods. These methods currently return
.B org.freedesktop.home1.NotSupported
because managed storage and lifecycle operations have not been implemented.
The
.B Changed
and
.B Removed
signals are declared for compatibility, but are not emitted by the current
implementation.
.SH D-BUS REGISTRATION AND LOGGING
At startup the daemon logs a startup message and logs successful registration
of the manager object at
.BR /org/freedesktop/home1 .
If it loses or cannot acquire its D-Bus name, it logs the event and schedules
a retry after 2500 milliseconds. Registration is attempted again when the
retry runs.
.PP
Messages are sent through syslog under the
.B homed
identifier and are handled by the system's configured logging service.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect the manager interface:
.PP
.nf
busctl --system introspect org.freedesktop.home1 /org/freedesktop/home1
.fi
.PP
Look up an account by name:
.PP
.nf
busctl --system call org.freedesktop.home1 /org/freedesktop/home1 org.freedesktop.home1.Manager GetHomeByName s root
.fi
.PP
Get the NSS-derived user record:
.PP
.nf
busctl --system call org.freedesktop.home1 /org/freedesktop/home1 org.freedesktop.home1.Manager GetUserRecordByName s root
.fi
.PP
Inspect a per-home object (replace
.I 0
with an existing UID):
.PP
.nf
busctl --system introspect org.freedesktop.home1 /org/freedesktop/home1/home/_0
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
.B homed
does not currently implement home creation or registration, storage backends,
encrypted home images, activation/deactivation, locking/unlocking, resizing,
home removal, full record parsing or validation, or Polkit-enforced
authorization for management operations. Do not rely on it to provide
systemd-homed storage or login-activation semantics.
.PP
The per-home object list is populated from NSS-visible accounts; it is not a
persistent registry of managed home areas.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/homed
Typical installed daemon path; the actual path depends on the Meson
.B libexecdir
setting.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/interfaces/org.freedesktop.home1.xml
Installed D-Bus interface description; the actual path depends on the Meson
.B datadir
setting.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR busctl (1),
.BR dbus-daemon (1),
.BR nsswitch.conf (5)
